WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.280 --> 00:00:06.520
 RStudio Cloud allows 
  us to create assignments for our learners 

00:00:06.520 --> 00:00:10.400
 via RStudio projects. 
  By creating assignments within an 

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:11.800
 RStudio Cloud workspace, 

00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:15.720
 we set up a shared environment 
  for our learners to access and complete 

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:18.840
 their work. Assignments in RStudio Cloud 

00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:22.600
 happen at the project level. 
  To create a new assignment 

00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:25.280
 we click on the new project 
  button here in the top right. 

00:00:26.040 --> 00:00:29.360
 Once we're inside our project, 
  we can create any files 

00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:32.800
 we'd like our students to use 
  as part of completing the assignment. 

00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:35.440
 This could include 
  an R Markdown document  

00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:39.000
 with instructions, an R script 
  with partially completed code, 

00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:43.160
 or any other type of file available to you 
  from within RStudio. 

00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:48.040
 After we create everything 
  needed to get an assignment together, 

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:52.080
 we want to make sure that our learners 
  can access it by clicking on the project 

00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:56.040
 settings button in the upper right, 
  clicking on the access panel, 

00:00:56.520 --> 00:01:00.160
 and from the who can view this project 
  dropdown menu, choosing everyone. 

00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:03.400
 The final step to 
  making this an assignment 

00:01:03.400 --> 00:01:06.400
 is to check the box 
  next to make this project an assignment. 

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:10.640
 When we navigate back to our workspace 
  by clicking on the workspace 

00:01:10.640 --> 00:01:14.520
 name at the top, we see that our project 
  is now listed as an assignment. 

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:19.400
 Our learners will see a corresponding tag 
  that says either start if they haven't 

00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:23.480
 yet opened the assignment or continue 
  if they've already opened the assignment. 

00:01:24.280 --> 00:01:27.280
 One thing to note is that if 
  we make changes to an assignment, 

00:01:27.560 --> 00:01:30.560
 they will not be applied 
  to any copies of the assignment 

00:01:30.560 --> 00:01:33.680
 that students have already created 
  by opening the assignment. 

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:37.440
 The changes we make to an assignment 
  will only apply to future 

00:01:37.440 --> 00:01:38.960
 copies of the assignment. 

